    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Farrell Auctioneers, Valuers & Estate Agents are delighted to bring to the market this pretty bungalow excellently located within walking distance to Kinvara village. The dwelling itself was built in c. 1973 and extends to approx. 1,200 sq ft and is an E energy rating. It sits on a corner site and the garden has many varieties of mature shrubs and trees and a beautiful fuchsiahedging, has a block built wall to sides of the house, a brick wall to the front with a single iron gate with a path leading to the light filled porch. There is a separate double iron gate providing access to the side of the house with parking and another double iron gate providing access to sheds and the rear of the property. The land at the rear has a stone wall boundary and iron farm gate for access. \n\nIts accommodation includes a large bright entrance porch, entrance hallway, kitchen / dining room, living room, sitting room, 4 bedrooms and a bathroom. \n\nThere are steps down to yard and sheds to the rear and a ramp and hand--rail at side door, The property has wall lights and a seating area on raised concrete plinth beside back door\n\nShed measurements:\n\nShed 1 280 x 400, galvanised roof, work bench, window and door with lock\n\nShed 2 450 x 320 galvanised roof over open area for refuse bins\n\nShed 3 560 x 400 galvanised roof, shelves workbench and double iron doors with lock and 150 cm lean-to shed\n\nThis property is ideally located within easy walking distance to the seaside village of Kinvara and its renowned cafés, restaurants, shops, schools, picturesque quay and all local amenities, the property also enjoys an excellent location just a 30-minute drive from Galway City, with easy access to the spectacular Burren National Park and the world-famous Wild Atlantic Way.\n\nViewing is recommended! to arrange a viewing email colm@colmfarrell.com or call 091 632688"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Porch - 1.9m (6'3\") x 3.18m (10'5\")\nThis area has UPVC doors and windows facing N & E, has tiled flooring, pine ceiling, double teak French doors to the hallway,\n\nEntrance Hall - 4.7m (15'5\") x 1.4m (4'7\")\nThis room has double French doors leads to sitting room, living room, bathroom and hot press has vinyl floor, ceiling rose and coving, facing an attractive carved door to bathroom\n\nLiving Room - 3.82m (12'6\") x 3.68m (12'1\")\nThis room is located just off the entrance hallway and a French door leads to the kitchen, has a ceiling rose, light fitting, vinyl floor and fireplace with tiled hearth and timber surround and gas fireplace.\n\nLiving Room Alcove - 3.08m (10'1\") x 1.6m (5'3\")\nThis alcove faces the front of the property, north facing and a large east facing aluminium window into the entrance porch, providing morning light, curtains and poles, vinyl floor\n\nSitting Room - 3.93m (12'11\") x 3.3m (10'10\")\nThis room has carpet flooring, wood surround fireplace with gas fire and North facing windows\n\nSide Porch - 0.95m (3'1\") x 0.95m (3'1\")\nThis area has tiled flooring and UPVC door and leads to side and rear of house\n\nKitchen Area (T Shape with Breakfast Bar) - 3.58m (11'9\") x 2.26m (7'5\")\nThis area has fitted wooden kitchen, stainless steel sink & mixer tap, tiled back splash, washing machine, gas hob and electric oven, coving, laminate counter top. Triple aspect windows, S,W & E, rose counter piece and light filling breakfast bar and entrance to side of house\n\nKitchen Area - 3.45m (11'4\") x 3.38m (11'1\")\nThis area has a N.W facing window, wood cabinets and long work top, breakfast bar centre light,wood panelling, semi solid floor, a rose centrepiece and French doors to living room.\n\nHall - 1.5m (4'11\") x 0.7m (2'4\")\nAccess to the hot press is located here\n\nHallway - 5.4m (17'9\") x 0.85m (2'9\")\nAccess to four bedrooms and attic\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.7m (8'10\") x 2.7m (8'10\")\nThis room is South facing, has carpet flooring and built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.6m (8'6\") x 2.67m (8'9\")\nThis room is South facing, is carpeted and has a fitted wardrobe and some wall shelves\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.74m (12'3\") x 2.67m (8'9\")\nThis room is south facing, carpet flooring and built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.3m (10'10\") x 3.9m (12'10\")\nThis room is North facing and has wood effect laminate flooring and built in wardrobes\n\nBathroom - 1.9m (6'3\") x 2.8m (9'2\")\nThis room faces the rear has two windows, a w.c. w.h.b. and vanity unit and mirror, shower and electric shower, T & G Ceiling, synthetic wall tiled wall covering\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
